    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0450" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894A.00/3–1247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-12T13:00:00+08:00">March 12, 1947—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 12—4:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>534. Reference my telegram 498, March 9. There is as yet no indication that
                    General Chen Yi will be removed as Governor General of Taiwan, as press reports
                    previously indicated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
